1
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:08,920
<i>Don't you think dreams are strange?</i>

2
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,840
<i>Sometimes they drift.</i>

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,079
<i>Sometimes they're a blur.</i>

4
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:18,960
<i>They seem so vivid,</i>

5
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:22,240
<i>but once you wake up, they're gone.</i>

6
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,640
<i>This is the story of a little cat,</i>

7
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:33,360
<i>kept in a cage where she wasn't</i>
<i>even allowed to dream.</i>

8
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:38,560
<i>Yet, she discovered something</i>
<i>more beautiful than anyone else ever had.</i>

9
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:47,320
<i>And perhaps this story</i>
<i>might help us answer a question.</i>

10
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:52,880
<i>But what was the question again?</i>

11
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:08,240
<i>We've always believed</i>

12
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:12,720
<i>that a good society needs</i>
<i>people with knowledge,</i>

13
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:15,400
<i>moral values,</i>
<i>and good manners.</i>

14
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:17,880
<i>That's why we</i>
<i>at Saint Cecilia School</i>

15
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:21,240
<i>are committed to nurturing our girls</i>
<i>into the finest young ladies.</i>

16
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:23,360
<i>Otherwise, we wouldn't</i>
<i>have been ranked</i>

17
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:25,400
<i>in the country's top five</i>
<i>for ten years.</i>

18
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:27,280
<i>We have to expand</i>

19
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:29,160
<i>our Hall of Fame</i>
<i>every year, you know.</i>

20
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:31,080
<i>As for our top students,</i>

21
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:33,600
<i>I'm proud of</i>
<i>every one of them.</i>

22
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:36,680
<i>What's that?</i>

23
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:39,760
<i>Who are this year's</i>
<i>top students?</i>

24
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:42,880
<i>Perhaps we shouldn't focus</i>
<i>so much on who's on top.</i>

25
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:44,080
<i>Equality, you know.</i>

26
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:45,560
<i>Everyone is equal.</i>

27
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:48,400
<i>The top students</i>
<i>in our school?</i>

28
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:49,520
<i>Which category</i>
<i>do you mean?</i>

29
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:53,760
<i>Grades, looks,</i>
<i>or how rich they are?</i>

30
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,920
<i>Well, they've got it all.</i>

31
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,600
<i>It's got to be</i>
<i>the Toxxxxin girls, right?</i>

32
00:01:58,400 --> 00:01:59,760
<i>Make sure you spell it with four X's.</i>

33
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:00,720
<i>There's Aidao.</i>

34
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:01,840
OUTSTANDING STUDENT

35
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,480
<i>Gale.</i>

36
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:07,280
<i>Chelsea and Meimei.</i>

37
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:08,880
<i>Four girls,</i>
<i>four different styles.</i>

38
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:10,160
<i>But one thing's for sure.</i>

39
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:13,360
<i>They're all gorgeous</i>
<i>and rich.</i>

40
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:14,600
<i>They're cool too, you know.</i>

41
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:17,040
<i>They dare to be different</i>
<i>and be themselves.</i>

42
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,800
<i>And they get good grades too.</i>

43
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:20,320
<i>Who could have a problem with that?</i>

44
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,240
<i>So, there was this</i>
<i>empty club room</i>

45
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:24,240
<i>at our school, right?</i>

46
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,240
<i>Then one day,</i>
<i>they just put up a sign</i>

47
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:27,760
<i>and claimed the whole room</i>
<i>for themselves.</i>

48
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:29,160
<i>Iconic.</i>

49
00:02:29,760 --> 00:02:31,920
<i>Why didn't the school</i>
<i>do anything?</i>

50
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,640
<i>There have been rumors,</i>
<i>you know.</i>

51
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:37,920
<i>They just get away</i>
<i>with everything.</i>

52
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,840
<i>Good for them.</i>
<i>This school is boring as hell.</i>

53
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:43,240
<i>They're total trendsetters.</i>

54
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:45,760
<i>They dare to do</i>
<i>what no one else will.</i>

55
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:47,360
<i>Seriously, they're my idols.</i>

56
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:50,160
<i>Yeah.</i>

57
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,920
<i>I guess I like</i>
<i>how mysterious they are too.</i>

58
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,560
<i>All their social media</i>
<i>is private.</i>

59
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:57,520
<i>Is that strange? Not really.</i>

60
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:59,640
<i>I guess that's just</i>
<i>how the elite are.</i>

61
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:00,960
<i>Especially Aidao.</i>

62
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:02,560
<i>You can barely</i>
<i>find anything about her.</i>

63
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,960
<i>But then,</i>
<i>look at her last name.</i>

64
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,280
AIDAO LAOSATHITPHONG

65
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:07,600
<i>If I had her last name,</i>

66
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:09,520
<i>I'd probably do the same.</i>

67
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:11,080
<i>Her family keeps</i>
<i>everything under wraps.</i>

68
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:27,640
Hey, now that you're defense minister,
I don't think you need to throw a party.

69
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:31,120
Why not save it for
when you become prime minister next term?

70
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:32,640
What do you say, Sathit?

71
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:36,760
You're giving me too much credit.

72
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:40,280
But having one on standby wouldn't hurt.

73
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:41,800
Sure.

74
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,120
You're quite the powerful family now.

75
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:47,760
Both father and son.

76
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:50,480
So, young man, your name's Din, right?

77
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,400
Yes, sir.

78
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:54,160
I hear you're top
of your political science class.

79
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,680
There aren't many major courses
in the first year, sir.

80
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:01,120
You already look promising.
Why not introduce him to the public?

81
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:03,680
Absolutely not. You know how it is.

82
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:06,360
These days, people on social media
are always ready to attack us.

83
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,800
I won't let Din go on social media
until he's truly ready.

84
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:15,440
Hey, don't be so strict with him.

85
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:20,079
Still, just don't do anything stupid.

86
00:04:20,959 --> 00:04:23,480
I can't be bothered laughing at you.

87
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:49,600
Don't put too much pressure on me.

88
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:51,160
Please.

89
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:53,920
All right, all right.

90
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,040
But I really can't help it.

91
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:01,760
There are quite a few black sheep
in my family,

92
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:04,120
so I have to be extra careful.

93
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:07,280
Isn't that right, Jes?

94
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,600
You never miss a chance
to take a dig at me

95
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:23,200
whenever this comes up, do you?

96
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,400
Am I wrong, though?

97
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:27,000
Good thing
you stopped using our last name.

98
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:29,320
I wouldn't dare cause trouble
for the Laosathitphong family.

99
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:34,440
Besides, my new last name
is much more stylish.

100
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,440
Jessada Wei.

101
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,480
Cool, huh?

102
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:46,320
Congratulations, big brother.

103
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:51,200
And congratulations to you too, Din.

104
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,880
Especially on your English score.

105
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:58,800
For a subject you struggle with,
that score was strangely good, wasn't it?

106
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:02,760
Hey, where are you going, Jes?

107
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:06,840
I'll go enjoy some peace and quiet,
like a black sheep should.

108
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:21,280
<i>Toxic.</i>

109
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,440
<i>Toxic.</i>

110
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,800
<i>Toxic.</i>

111
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:48,560
What kind of high school kid takes exams
for a university student like you?

112
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:51,680
You know, you could knock first, Uncle.

113
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:56,040
And that's what we call a fair trade.

114
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:59,280
When my dear brother
asks his little sister for help,

115
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,720
I have to make him owe me.

116
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:05,560
It might come in handy someday.

117
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,720
You're good at making people owe you.

118
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,000
Just like you do with me, right?

119
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:12,240
Of course.

120
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:17,000
Here's that Summer Trend questionnaire

121
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:19,600
you asked me to get
the younger kids at school to fill out.

122
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:25,040
You're getting better at this every day.

123
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:31,040
I'd rather have your help
than your praise.

124
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:34,480
What are you talking about?
I have no idea what you mean.

125
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:35,880
What do you want from me?

126
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:37,920
My record collection? Go pick something.

127
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,520
Come on, no. I need the usual favor.

128
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,120
Keep a lookout for me.

129
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:48,280
The Toxxxxin girls have plans
to go wild today.

130
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:52,120
I'm counting on you.

131
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:57,480
These crazy wildcats.

132
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:13,160
Hey! What the hell happened?

133
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,559
<i>Do I think</i>
<i>the Toxxxxin girls go wild</i>

134
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:38,960
<i>when they're</i>
<i>outside school?</i>

135
00:08:39,679 --> 00:08:41,320
<i>No way.</i>

136
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:47,360
<i>Their grades are so good.</i>

137
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:50,440
<i>I bet studying alone</i>
<i>keeps them busy.</i>

138
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,680
<i>Hobbies?</i>

139
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:04,400
<i>I'm sure they have some. But probably</i>
<i>something fancy and expensive.</i>

140
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,440
<i>I'm kind of curious too.</i>

141
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:07,800
<i>Like, glamorous princess stuff?</i>

142
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:09,680
<i>It must be fabulous.</i>

143
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:47,200
Tonight was fucking amazing.

144
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:48,120
Seriously.

145
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:53,200
Hey, are the younger kids
making content about us again?

146
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:55,160
Everyone's suddenly talking about us.

147
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:58,400
The advertising club again?

148
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:01,640
What are they saying this time?

149
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:05,160
Same old stuff.

150
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:09,080
They're guessing
what the Toxxxxin girls' lives are like.

151
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:12,760
"They must have
loads of celebrity friends."

152
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:15,360
"They probably live
super luxurious lives."

153
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:18,160
"They must get to do whatever they want."

154
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,360
Do whatever we want?

155
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:23,120
Yeah, right.

156
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:26,760
Things are probably about to get
even tougher for Princess Aidao.

157
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:30,200
Your dad's a minister now.

158
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:35,040
I mean, sure.
I'm absolutely happy.

159
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:39,360
Doesn't that call for a toast?

160
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:44,920
Congratulations to
Colonel Sathit Laosathitphong.

161
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,760
Cheers!

162
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:02,520
Ugh, this sucks!

163
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:08,240
What the hell are you doing?

164
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:21,320
Guys.

165
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:24,480
Thanks for everything.

166
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:28,960
For sneaking out with me
and keeping your accounts private,

167
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:30,400
even though

168
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:34,080
you're not being forced to like I am.

169
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:36,280
Come on.

170
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:39,320
We're not that different.

171
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:40,240
Exactly.

172
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:42,160
They don't have to force us.

173
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:43,800
We don't really have a choice anyway.

174
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,960
Damn, our lives are just…

175
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:53,320
We seem to have everything…

176
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:57,240
but we don't get a say in anything.

177
00:11:58,240 --> 00:11:59,880
We can't choose.

178
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:02,120
We can't think for ourselves.

179
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:04,640
We can't decide our own futures.

180
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:08,600
We're not even

181
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,000
allowed to dream.

182
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:17,840
Enough with the drama.

183
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:20,920
Yeah.

184
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,160
Cheer up! Cheer up!

185
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:24,360
Meimei!

186
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:28,280
- It's not me who needs cheering up.
- Who cares?

187
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,080
I don't freaking know!

188
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,160
Aidao?

189
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:38,320
Don't worry about the dreams.

190
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,560
You have every right to dream.

191
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:45,480
Who can stop us from dreaming?

192
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:48,400
Exactly.

193
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:52,640
Our dreams are where we're most free.

194
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:59,040
Speaking of this, Aidao,
your dreams are the spiciest, aren't they?

195
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:01,680
Those weird dreams you told us about,

196
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:03,640
do you still have them?

197
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:09,320
Well…

198
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:12,360
I do, almost every day.

199
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:13,880
Aww. Seriously?

200
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:16,760
I told you. I've been saying it all along.

201
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,400
It's a sign.

202
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:21,680
Stop putting ideas in her head.
You're always so dramatic.

203
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:24,320
I'm not being dramatic.
It really is romantic.

204
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:26,480
Meimei!

205
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,280
What?

206
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:34,200
<i>Yes, I've been having strange dreams</i>
<i>for a long time.</i>

207
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:41,560
<i>Even though I have them often,</i>

208
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:44,800
<i>the details are hazy</i>
<i>and hard to piece together.</i>

209
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:52,200
<i>All I know is that</i>
<i>there's always a girl I've never met.</i>

210
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:58,000
<i>And every time,</i>
<i>my heart races like it never has before.</i>

211
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,720
<i>At first, I was excited.</i>

212
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:06,040
<i>It felt like that girl</i>
<i>gave me something to hope for.</i>

213
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:09,880
<i>But as time went on,</i>

214
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:14,680
<i>I began to feel</i>
<i>it was too beautiful to be real.</i>

215
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:20,960
<i>It was just a fantasy</i>
<i>I'd created to fool myself.</i>

216
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:28,800
<i>Even so, I couldn't help thinking,</i>

217
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:31,720
<i>"I want to meet her so badly."</i>

218
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,440
- Shit!
- Quick, help her!

219
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:39,160
- Help her!
- I'll jump in.

220
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,680
Hey. Are you hurt?

221
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:10,720
What the heck are you doing here?

222
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:16,680
I was just walking around here,
and I fell in.

223
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:18,120
What do you mean, walking around?!

224
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:20,040
Do you really expect us to believe that?

225
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,800
Hey. Calm down.

226
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:23,800
Let me talk to her.

227
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:34,440
What happened?

228
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,760
Please tell me.

229
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:41,480
JUNJAI JANYAKUL

230
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:54,040
Hey, you're sure nobody saw us?

231
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,600
Yes. I checked.

232
00:16:57,720 --> 00:17:03,720
Okay, let's recap what just happened.

233
00:17:13,319 --> 00:17:14,240
I'm sorry.

234
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:31,080
Why are you blushing?

235
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:37,720
So, what were you doing here?

236
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:41,760
I just wandered over here

237
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,040
and fell in.

238
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:46,000
Oh, please.

239
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:47,760
We could tell you're lying even from Mars.

240
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:48,960
It's true.

241
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:50,680
And you don't need to worry.

242
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:52,560
I'm completely fine. I should get going.

243
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:54,200
Bye. Thank you.

244
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:01,440
That was bad.

245
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:02,720
It really was.

246
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:06,200
<i>And when we pulled her out again,</i>

247
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:08,320
<i>she just burst into tears.</i>

248
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:12,640
<i>After that, she wouldn't say another word.</i>

249
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,160
<i>It was so weird.</i>

250
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:18,800
<i>At least she let us take her home.</i>

251
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:24,120
And luckily, she exchanged
contact details with Aidao.

252
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:26,240
Otherwise,
I wouldn't be able to sleep tonight.

253
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:27,320
Right?

254
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:30,120
JUNJAI, WHENEVER YOU'RE READY TO TALK,
LET ME KNOW.

255
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:32,000
PHONE CALL, VIDEO CALL

256
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:33,360
Hey.

257
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:34,280
Huh?

258
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:36,880
Yeah, exactly.

259
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:38,920
So what do we do now?

260
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:43,200
We don't even know who she is.

261
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:44,680
I checked.

262
00:18:44,760 --> 00:18:46,520
Her name's Junjai Janyakul.

263
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:47,680
Grade 11, Class 1.

264
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:50,240
She's from Lampang. She just
transferred here on a scholarship.

265
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:52,360
That was fast. Classic Gale.

266
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:56,040
Still, that doesn't tell us
what she was doing there.

267
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:59,040
But seriously…

268
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:02,800
There aren't many possibilities, right?

269
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:07,360
Guys.

270
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:09,920
It's bothering me.

271
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:14,120
Let's go to the Grade 11 building
tomorrow.

272
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:16,840
But let's keep it low-key.

273
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:19,400
I don't want to draw attention.

274
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:23,920
Won't we draw attention
just by showing up?

275
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:29,240
GUYS!!!! THE TOXXXXIN GIRLS ARE
AT THE GRADE 11 BUILDING!

276
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:31,320
<i>Have you seen this girl?</i>

277
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,000
<i>Gosh!</i>

278
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,280
I'M DYING! #TOXXXXIN

279
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,920
<i>She's upstairs.</i>

280
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,400
- #TOXXXXIN
- MY HEART CAN'T TAKE THIS.

281
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:39,920
THEY'RE SO FREAKING GORGEOUS IN PERSON.

282
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,880
ARE THEY HERE LOOKING FOR SOMEONE?

283
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:45,760
- WHO'S THE LUCKY ONE?
- OR DID SOMEONE PISS THEM OFF?

284
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,640
- I WISH IT WERE ME.
- WE'RE ALL HAVING GAY PANIC!

285
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:54,680
Oh, JJ?

286
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,680
Of course, we know her.

287
00:19:56,760 --> 00:19:58,000
She's in our class.

288
00:19:58,080 --> 00:20:00,000
We're not close, though.

289
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:02,240
Did she cause you any trouble?

290
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:04,360
Oh, no. Nothing like that.

291
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:06,720
Do you know who she's close to?

292
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:09,040
No one, really.

293
00:20:10,320 --> 00:20:14,680
Wait. Did you just call her JJ?

294
00:20:14,760 --> 00:20:18,320
Yeah. JJ, as in "jing jok," a house gecko.

295
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:22,480
Doesn't she look like one?

296
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:26,960
But we didn't come up with it.

297
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:28,360
Everyone in our class calls her that.

298
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:33,080
Then can you tell me who came up with it?

299
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:37,760
Hey.

300
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:47,400
- What happened?
- Oh, something just dropped, ma'am.

301
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:49,040
Just dropped? That was so loud.

302
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:50,600
Move aside. Let me take a look.

303
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:52,720
- You really can't go in, ma'am.
- Girls, I said move aside.

304
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:54,920
It's really nothing.
Really, ma'am.

305
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:55,920
Ma'am.

306
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,560
- Please don't go in.
- Move aside.

307
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:00,320
It's really nothing, ma'am.

308
00:21:00,400 --> 00:21:01,920
Someone just dropped something.

309
00:21:02,680 --> 00:21:04,200
Please, ma'am.

310
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:06,320
- You can't go in.
- There's really nothing.

311
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:08,320
Girls, I said move aside.

312
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:11,680
Ma'am, something's happened!
A student fainted in the gym.

313
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:13,680
Please come with me.

314
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:15,640
Hurry.

315
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:22,360
Hey!

316
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:23,560
Let her go.

317
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:27,160
Let's focus on this.

318
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:43,520
I bet Aidao's dying to know
who that girl is.

319
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:50,000
The girl we met yesterday is
Ploypim Chiaotrakhul.

320
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:51,320
DONATED BY THE CHIAOTRAKHUL FAMILY

321
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:53,600
Grade 11. She's in Junjai's class.

322
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:55,760
Rich family, top student.

323
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:57,760
Her family's in real estate.

324
00:21:57,840 --> 00:22:00,440
Her dad donated so much money
to the school

325
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:03,200
